# Enterprise-wide Staff and product ships

When a change is something the **whole enterprise** would need or benefit from (shared Staff tooling, CMS patterns, platform ops, content editors, auth gates, and similar), do **not** ship it to only one brand or one marketing site.

## Required ship path

1. **Author in the main shared product app** (`~/pavilion` / commons-pto-demo Staff + APIs) first.
2. **Expose it on every applicable Brand / Platform Staff surface** (Pavilion, Business Rocket, AuraFlux), product-scoped when content or orgs differ.
3. **Pull into that company’s marketing site and customers when applicable** (commons-site, Business Rocket web, customer promote / SHMS) so the feature is usable end-to-end, not stuck on demo alone.

## Do not confuse with customer Client Staff

School / client **Client Staff** gets enterprise capabilities when they apply to customer builds (for example Blog), gated by **Modules** check/uncheck so Brand Staff can turn them on or off per org.

Company-only fleet ops stay on **Brand / Platform Staff**.

## Anti-patterns (forbidden)

- Building shared Brand Staff tooling only for Pavilion Platform mode and leaving BR/AF without it
- Shipping Staff CRUD without a public/read path for the site that should consume it (when applicable)
- Treating a demo-only deploy as “done for the enterprise” when sister brands or customer trees also need the same capability
